<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61094" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυρτ-ότης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>humped shoulders, stoop</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Πλάτωνος κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.26b
				</span></i>
			; <i>convex surface</i> of a bone, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				2.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.5
			</span></i> (pl.), al.; of the spherical moon, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.922d
			</span></i>; of the earth, <i><span class="en">
				Cleom.
				1.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς θαλάσσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					1.1.20
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theo Sm.
				p.123
			</span></i> H. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>convexity</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιλότης</span>,
			of a line, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				217b3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mete.</u>
				386a1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Spir.</u>
				1.23
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
